    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A northern British kingdom formed from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/picts">Picts</a> and Gaelic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dal-riata">Dál Riata</a>, traditionally dated to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kenneth-macalpin">Kenneth MacAlpin</a> around 843.</li><li>It kept its independence against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> in the Wars of Independence, won by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/robert-the-bruce">Robert the Bruce</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-bannockburn">Bannockburn</a> in 1314.</li><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/james-vi-and-i">James VI</a> inherited <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> in 1603, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/acts-of-union-1707">Acts of Union</a> of 1707 merged the two kingdoms into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-great-britain">Great Britain</a>.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/james-ii-of-scotland">James II of Scotland</a>, an enthusiast for artillery, was killed in 1460 when one of his own <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/field-artillery">cannons</a> burst during the siege of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roxburgh-castle">Roxburgh Castle</a>.</p></aside>
    </section>

